[48.589101, "o", "The tool ran successfully (exit code 2 = BLOCK) and produced a complete, signed report. Here is the full breakdown:\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🚫 Preflight Verdict: BLOCK — upgrade must not proceed\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Run Metadata\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Verdict** | `BLOCK` |\r\n| **Fingerprint** | `287c21b99ee3e4bec65205865842c87e4684a874ff1fe8e74e69b03cd68ee605` |\r\n| **Tool** | helm-agent-preflight `v0.1.0` (commit `91250d3`) |\r\n| **No deployment occurred** | ✅ confirmed (`true`) |\r\n| **Offline mode** | ✅ `true` |\r\n| **Rendering stability** | ✅ confirmed |\r\n| **Evidence completeness** | ✅ `COMPLETE` (no limitations) |\r\n| **Timestamp (UTC)** | `2026-11-13T03:49:15Z` |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Diff Summary\r\n- **Modified**: 1 resource — `ClusterRole/webapp-reader`\r\n- **Added**: 0\r\n- **Removed**: 0\r\n\r\nThe single change expanded `$.rules` from narrow, explicit permissions to full wildcards across all three dimensions.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 🔴 Security Findings (2 × CRITICAL)\r\n\r\n#### Finding 1 — RBAC-001\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Rule** | `RBAC-001` |\r\n| **Severity** | `CRITICAL` |\r\n| **Object** | `ClusterRole / webapp-reader` |\r\n| **JSON Path** | `$.rules[0].resources` |\r\n| **Message** | Wildcard `*` in resources grants access to all resource types |\r\n| **Pre-existing** | ❌ No (introduced by this upgrade) |\r\n\r\n#### Finding 2 — RBAC-002\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Rule** | `RBAC-002` |\r\n| **Severity** | `CRITICAL` |\r\n| **Object** | `ClusterRole / webapp-reader` |\r\n| **JSON Path** | `$.rules[0].verbs` |\r\n| **Message** | Wildcard `*` in verbs grants all operations |\r\n| **Pre-existing** | ❌ No (introduced by this upgrade) |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Root Cause\r\n\r\nThe candidate chart changed `ClusterRole/webapp-reader` from this safe baseline:\r\n```yaml\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n…to this dangerously over-permissive candidate:\r\n```yaml\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n    resources: [\"*\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 🔧 Smallest Concrete Fix\r\n\r\nRevert the `ClusterRole` rules in the candidate chart back to the explicit, least-privilege set from the baseline. Edit the candidate's template (e.g. `examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/clusterrole.yaml`) to replace the wildcard rule:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# BEFORE (candidate — blocked)\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n    resources: [\"*\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# AFTER (fixed — matches principle of least privilege)\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf the application legitimately needs access to additional resources or verbs, enumerate them **explicitly** (e.g. `[\"pods\", \"services\", \"configmaps\"]`) — never use `*` wildcards in a ClusterRole.\r\n\r\nOnce the candidate chart is corrected, re-run preflight and obtain a PASS verdict (with its fingerprint) before proceeding with the upgrade. Human authorization is required before modifying any project files.\r\n"]
